    "summary": "Cloth, woman&#039;s wrapper, composed of ten identical hand-woven strips of hand-spun cotton, hand-sewn together selvedge to selvedge. Both the warp and the weft use white (natural-coloured) and a dark shade of indigo cotton in lines along and across the cloth to create a checked plaid pattern. The strip along the top of the cloth is longer than others and has an extension at the end to form a tuck-in tie fastener. The warp ends have been hemmed by hand-sewing.",
